labwc-tabs.patch: Fluxbox-style window tabs for labwc 0.20.2 (kflux).
Licence: GPL-2.0-only, like labwc, which it modifies.

Design: decisions/0004-tabs-in-labwc.md in the kflux repository.
New: src/tabs.c, include/tabs.h. Hooks: view visibility/focusability, frame-state
handoff (view_take_frame_state), titlebar tab strip (ssd-titlebar.c), focus
redirect (desktop.c), foreign-toplevel retargeting, StartTabbing outline drag
(interactive.c, cursor.c, overlay.c), actions ActivateTab, NextTab, PreviousTab,
GoToTab, MoveTabLeft, MoveTabRight, DetachTab, StartTabbing,
GroupWithWindowBelow, JoinTabGroup (action.c, labwc-actions.5).
Apply with: patch -Np1 -i labwc-tabs.patch (in labwc-0.20.2/).

diff --git a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
index 3414247..277c9a3 100644
--- a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
+++ b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
@@ -412,6 +412,51 @@ Actions are used in menus and keyboard/mouse bindings.
 	Use together with the WarpCursor action to not just hide the cursor but
 	to additionally move it away to prevent e.g. hover effects.
 
+*<action name="ActivateTab" />*
+	Switch to the tab under the pointer. Only useful in a "Title" or
+	"TitleBar" mousebind, typically after Focus and Raise.
+
+	Windows can be grouped into tabs, as in Fluxbox: a group shares one
+	frame and only its active window is shown. The others are hidden from
+	the window switcher and from taskbars, and the titlebar shows one tab
+	per window. Moving, resizing, maximizing, minimizing and sending the
+	frame to another workspace act on the whole group. Only windows with a
+	server-side titlebar can be grouped.
+
+*<action name="NextTab" />*++
+*<action name="PreviousTab" />*
+	Switch to the next or previous tab of the active window's group,
+	wrapping around.
+
+*<action name="GoToTab" index="value" />*
+	Switch to the tab at *index* (1 is the first; negative values count
+	from the last).
+
+*<action name="MoveTabLeft" />*++
+*<action name="MoveTabRight" />*
+	Move the active tab one place left or right in its group.
+
+*<action name="DetachTab" />*
+	Take the active window out of its group into a window of its own.
+
+*<action name="StartTabbing" />*
+	Start dragging an outline of the window. Dropped on another window's
+	titlebar, the window joins that window's group as its active tab;
+	dropped anywhere else, it leaves its group (if any) and moves there.
+	Use in a "Title" or "TitleBar" Drag mousebind, for example with the
+	Ctrl modifier as in Fluxbox.
+
+*<action name="GroupWithWindowBelow" />*
+	Add the topmost window beneath the active one that it overlaps (or, if
+	none overlaps, the next window down) to the active window's group, in
+	the background.
+
+*<action name="JoinTabGroup" identifier="value" />*
+	Join the group of the topmost visible window on the current workspace
+	whose identifier matches the glob *value*. Intended for window rules,
+	to group windows automatically when they first map. Does nothing if the
+	window is already grouped.
+
 *<action name="EnableScrollWheelEmulation" />*++
 *<action name="DisableScrollWheelEmulation" />*++
 *<action name="ToggleScrollWheelEmulation">*
